 for bestpractices and # Project Detail Prompt

Target: LifeOps — Modular Multi-Agent AI Operating System

This prompt is intended for an AI development tool to build the Project Detail page and its connected features end-to-end. It enforces runtime safety, UI/UX standards, and a robust backend/frontend stack that guards against null/undefined values before array operations, uses proper default states, and validates API responses as described in the project’s mandatory coding standards.

---

## Overview

Build a comprehensive, developer-centric "Project Detail" experience for LifeOps. This deep-dive page presents a specific project's roadmap, backlog, agent jobs, run history, and release artifacts. It integrates with Storage & Artifacts for artifact storage (with signed URLs and retention policies) and with the Projects Module for automation (roadmaps, ticket triage, PR management, release automation, and CI/CD triggers). The page is part of a larger Developer Dashboard ecosystem that includes a Projects Dashboard with roadmaps, tickets, PRs, releases, and automation templates.

Key outcomes:
- Provide an actionable, unified view of a single project, with fast access to artifacts, run histories, and agent-led workflows.
- Ensure secure, auditable storage/retention for artifacts and logs.
- Enable governance for automation with approvals, constraints, and safety rails.
- Deliver a consistent, dark-mode-first UI aligned with the design system and accessible, scalable components.

---

## Page Description (Full Detail)

What this page is:
- A dedicated, read-only/editable deep-dive page for one project in LifeOps, surfacing:
  - Roadmap: milestones, timelines, ownership, status, and editor for milestone updates.
  - Backlog: prioritized tickets, triage status, assignees, and filters (status, priority, tag, sprint/iteration).
  - Agent Jobs: timeline/list of agent-initiated actions, pending approvals, handoffs, and inter-agent communications.
  - Run History: historical runs of agent workflows, with status, duration, results, and traceability.
  - Release Artifacts: viewer/list of artifacts, diffs, logs, and generated content; with signed URLs for secure access and retention policy indicators.
- Interconnected with:
  - Storage & Artifacts: signed URLs, controlled access, lifecycle retention (e.g., 30/60/90 days or policy-driven).
  - Projects Module: automation workflows (roadmaps, ticket triage, PR management, release automation, CI/CD triggers).
- UI goals:
  - Quick-glance project health metrics in header.
  - Tabbed sections for Roadmap, Backlog, Agent Jobs, Run History, Artifacts.
  - Actionable controls for edits, approvals, artifact downloads, and run replays.
  - Rich search, filtering, and sorting across backlog and runs.
  - Visual guidance via compact charts (timeline, burn-down/velocity, run success rate) on dark background.
- API integrations:
  - No external APIs required beyond the internal system; all endpoints simulated or connected to LifeOps services (Storage, Automation, CI/CD, Agent Orchestration). Ensure robust error handling and data validation.

UI/UX guidance:
- Visual emphasis on clarity, traceability, and control.
- Use cards, tabs, and modular sections with consistent spacing (12-column grid, 24–32px gutters).
- Preserve accessibility: sufficient contrast, keyboard navigability, and screen-reader friendly structure.
- Favor performance: lazy-load heavy sections (Artifacts previews, large run histories) and paginate long lists.

---

## Components to Build

1) ProjectDetailHeaderCard
- Displays project name, status, last updated, integrations status, and quick actions (edit roadmap, trigger run, export config).
- Data inputs: project object with id, name, status, healthScore, integrationsStatus.
- Behavior: collapses/expands metrics; shows signed URLs for artifacts when applicable.

2) RoadmapPanel
- Timeline with milestones, due dates, owners, and status.
- Inline milestone editor (add/edit/delete) with validation.
- Drag-and-drop reordering within a sprint/roadmap (optional).
- Data shape: roadmap: { milestones: [{ id, title, dueDate, status, owner, notes }] }

3) BacklogPanel
- Ticket list with filters: status, priority, assignee, tag, sprint.
- Card-based tickets with actions: triage, assign, link PR, mark as done.
- Search bar and multi-select filters.
- Data shape: tickets: Array of { id, title, status, priority, assignee, tags, sprint, createdAt }

4) AgentJobsPanel
- List or timeline of agent-initiated actions, with status (pending, running, completed, failed), initiatedAt, dueAt.
- Approvals queue for actions requiring user review.
- Detail drawer or modal for each job with traceability path (handoffs, messages).
- Data shape: jobs: Array of { id, agentName, action, status, startedAt, endedAt, traceId, needsApproval }

5) RunHistoryPanel
- Historical runs for the project’s automation, with status, duration, result summary, and link to artifacts/logs.
- Filters by date range, status.
- Optional chart: run success rate over time.
- Data shape: runs: Array of { id, runDate, status, durationMs, resultSummary, traceId }

6) ArtifactsPanel
- Artifact listing with artifact type (artifact/diff/log/generated content), size, createdAt, retention policy tag.
- Preview pane with signed URL fetch, download button, and view (viewer or raw).
- Diff viewer and snippet previews; per-artifact access with signed URLs.
- Data shape: artifacts: Array of { id, type, name, createdAt, sizeBytes, retentionPolicy, signedUrl }

7) Storage & Artifacts Integration Connector (Internal)
- Service calls to storage layer to fetch lists, generate signed URLs, and apply retention policies.
- Ensure data safety with data ?? [] defaults and array guards.

8) ProjectsModuleAutomationPanel (Automation templates & CI/CD)
- Section for roadmaps, PR triage templates, release automation templates, and CI/CD triggers.
- Create/edit automation templates; trigger manual runs; set permissions and constraints.
- Data shape: templates: Array of { id, type, config, permissions, constraints }

9) Security & Audit Drawer
- Access logs, action history, role-based permissions for edits and runs.
- Display reversible actions and an audit trail with trace IDs.

10) Empty State / Onboarding Cards
- For empty roadmaps, backlog, or runs with guided prompts.

11) Global Utilities
- Date/Time pickers, currency/spend controls for automation budgets, and timezones aware cron scheduling (for CronJobs equivalent).

---

## Implementation Requirements

### Frontend

- Frameworks: React + TypeScript (prefer Next.js or a similar framework for routing).
- State Management: Use React hooks with proper defaults; arrays initialized as useState<Type[]>([]); avoid null state.
- Components:
  - Reusable Card component with consistent shadow, borders, padding, hover states.
  - Tabs component for Project Detail sections.
  - FilterBar component for Backlog and RunHistory with debounce-safe search.
  - Modal/Drawer components for artifact viewing and job detail.
  - Avatar/AvatarGroup for owners/assignees.
- Data Handling:
  - All API responses validated: const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : [].
  - Use data ?? [] for any list derived from API responses (e.g., const tickets = data?.tickets ?? []).
  - Guard all array calls: (array ?? []).map(...), Array.isArray(array) ? array.map(...) : [].
- API integration:
  - Mocked or real internal API endpoints for: getProjectDetail, getRoadmap, getBacklog, getAgentJobs, getRunHistory, getArtifacts, getTemplates, and signed URL generation.
- Security & Accessibility:
  - Role-based access for editing roadmaps and approving actions.
  - Keyboard navigable, accessible labels, aria attributes.
- Performance:
  - Use pagination or infinite scroll for long lists (Backlog, RunHistory).
  - Lazy load heavy components (Artifacts previews, large run histories).

### Backend

- Data Models (PostgreSQL or equivalent):
  - projects: id, name, description, status, health_score, created_at, updated_at, integrations
  - roadmaps: id, project_id, milestone_id, title, due_date, status, owner_id, notes
  - milestones: id, roadmap_id, title, due_date, status
  - tickets: id, project_id, title, description, status, priority, assignee_id, tags, sprint, created_at, updated_at
  - agents: id, name, version, status
  - jobs: id, project_id, agent_id, action, status, started_at, ended_at, trace_id, needs_approval
  - runs: id, project_id, run_date, status, duration_ms, trace_id, result_summary
  - artifacts: id, project_id, type, name, created_at, size_bytes, retention_policy, signed_url
  - templates: id, type, config_json, permissions, constraints_json, created_at
- Functions/Procedures:
  - generateSignedUrl(artifact_id, expiration): returns URL with signed token
  - getRetentionPolicy(project_id): returns policy object
  - validateAndRecordAction(actionPayload): ensures constraints, safety rails, approvals
- API Endpoints (CRUD-ish, with proper validation):
  - GET /api/projects/{projectId} -> ProjectDetail
  - GET /api/projects/{projectId}/roadmap
  - POST /api/projects/{projectId}/roadmap/milestones
  - GET /api/projects/{projectId}/backlog
  - PATCH /api/projects/{projectId}/backlog/{ticketId}
  - GET /api/projects/{projectId}/agents/jobs
  - GET /api/projects/{projectId}/runs
  - GET /api/projects/{projectId}/artifacts
  - POST /api/artifacts/{artifactId}/signed-url
  - GET /api/projects/{projectId}/templates
  - POST /api/cronjobs (for scheduling automation) and GET /api/cronjobs/{id}
- Validation & Safety:
  - Validate all inputs; enforce types and required fields.
  - Use allow-list for actions requiring approvals; implement safety rails as per Master Dashboard definitions.
  - All operations must be auditable; store trace IDs, user, timestamp, and rationale.

### Integration

- Data flow:
  - Frontend consumes normalized API responses; uses data ?? [] with Array.isArray guards.
  - Artifacts panel uses signed URLs provided by backend; if not present, calls generateSignedUrl as needed.
  - Roadmap edits propagate to RoadmapPanel via API mutations; backlog edits reflect in Tickets service.
  - CronJobs/Automation section connects to ProjectsModule for templates and triggers; approvals flow routes through Approvals queue.
- Consistency:
  - Consistent data shapes across panels.
  - Central error handling and toast/notification system for success/error states.
- Security:
  - JWT/OAuth-based authentication; endpoints validate user roles.
  - Signed URL lifetime configurable by retention policies.

---

## User Experience Flow

1) Access Project Detail
- User lands on the Project Detail page for a selected project from Projects Dashboard.
- Page header shows project name, health status, and integration indicators.
- Quick actions: Edit Roadmap, Create Run, Export Config, and Jump to Artifacts.

2) Roadmap Interaction
- User views milestones in a timeline.
- User adds/edits milestones via inline editor or modal; validation ensures due dates, owners, and statuses.
- Milestones update in real-time via API; roadmap timeline refreshes.

3) Backlog Management
- User filters backlog by status/priority/assignee/tags/sprint.
- User searches tickets; results render in cards with summary and actions (triage, assign, link PR).
- User updates ticket status or assigns owners; changes persist via API.

4) Agent Jobs & Approvals
- User views agent jobs timeline; pending approvals appear in Approvals queue.
- User reviews details in a drawer/modal; approves or requests changes; actions are logged.

5) Run History
- User browses runs; can filter by date/status and view run details.
- User opens a run to see trace, duration, results, and links to logs/artifacts.

6) Artifacts & Diffs
- User lists artifacts; selects an artifact to view or download via signed URL.
- Diffs, generated content, and logs accessible with appropriate permissions.
- Artifacts retention status is visible; user can request policy updates if permitted.

