## User Experience Flow

1) Access Project Detail
- User lands on the Project Detail page for a selected project from Projects Dashboard.
- Page header shows project name, health status, and integration indicators.
- Quick actions: Edit Roadmap, Create Run, Export Config, and Jump to Artifacts.

2) Roadmap Interaction
- User views milestones in a timeline.
- User adds/edits milestones via inline editor or modal; validation ensures due dates, owners, and statuses.
- Milestones update in real-time via API; roadmap timeline refreshes.

3) Backlog Management
- User filters backlog by status/priority/assignee/tags/sprint.
- User searches tickets; results render in cards with summary and actions (triage, assign, link PR).
- User updates ticket status or assigns owners; changes persist via API.

4) Agent Jobs & Approvals
- User views agent jobs timeline; pending approvals appear in Approvals queue.
- User reviews details in a drawer/modal; approves or requests changes; actions are logged.

5) Run History
- User browses runs; can filter by date/status and view run details.
- User opens a run to see trace, duration, results, and links to logs/artifacts.

6) Artifacts & Diffs
- User lists artifacts; selects an artifact to view or download via signed URL.
- Diffs, generated content, and logs accessible with appropriate permissions.
- Artifacts retention status is visible; user can request policy updates if permitted.

7) Automation & Templates
- User browses automation templates (roadmaps, PR triage, CI/CD triggers).
- User creates/edits templates; defines constraints, safety rails, and approval rules.

8) Audit & Security
- User accesses audit drawer to review action history and traceability.

